ests the opponent likely does not have a strong hand like a Flush or Top Pair (Queen). My pair of 6s has reasonable showdown value against random high cards or lower pairs (like a pair of 5s or 2s). Betting here has little utility; worse hands will fold, and better hands (like a higher pair or a rivered 9) will call. Checking allows me to realize my equity and get to showdown without risking more chips in a spot where I am likely ahead but vulnerable to being raised or called by better.\n\nReason: I have a marginal made hand (pair of 6s) in a small pot. The opponent has shown no aggression. Checking is the safest option to reach a showdown and win against weaker hands without opening myself up to a raise or betting into a better hand.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
